        "valueString": "No deformity, erythema, or swelling. Tenderness at anterolateral shoulder (subacromial/greater tuberosity region); no AC joint or bony tenderness. Active abduction limited to approximately 90–100 degrees by pain, with painful arc from 70–110 degrees. Passive range of motion slightly greater but still painful. Jobe/empty can test painful with preserved power; Hawkins impingement test positive."
